==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|bataillon|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/bəˈtælɪən/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|military|lang=en}} An [[army]] [[unit]] having two or more [[company|companies]], etc. and a [[headquarters]]. Traditionally forming part of a [[regiment]].
# {{context|US|military|lang=en}} an army unit having two or more companies, etc. and a headquarters; forming part of a [[brigade]].
# Any large [[body]] of [[troops]].
# {{context|by extension|lang=en}} A [[great]] [[number]] of things.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|great number of things}} [[heap]], [[horde]], [[load]], [[mass]], [[pile]], [[swathe]]

